<title>ITALY: Bank of Italy sets 9.0 trillion lire repo tender.</title>
<headline>Bank of Italy sets 9.0 trillion lire repo tender.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Italy said it called a 9.0 trillion lire repurchase tender for today or tomorrow for government securities to be resold on January 2, 1997.</p>
<p>At the previous comparable operation for 14.0 trillion lire on December 16, the minimum accepted rate stood at 7.58 percent and the average rate at 7.38 percent.</p>
